  "prediction": "**Dry Ice Bomb Incident at Disneyland**\n\nA 22-year-old Disneyland employee, Christian Barnes, has been arrested in connection with the detonation of a dry ice bomb in the park's Toontown area. The explosion occurred on Tuesday evening, forcing the evacuation of the area for two hours. Fortunately, no one was injured in the incident.\n\nAccording to Anaheim police, Barnes, who worked as an outdoor vendor, placed dry ice in a trash can, which caused the explosion. Detectives found fragments of a water bottle in the trash can, suggesting that Barnes used the dry ice to create the explosion.\n\nBarnes was arrested on suspicion of possessing a destructive device and is being held on $1 million bail. He is cooperating with investigators and has indicated that the incident was an isolated one with unanticipated impacts.\n\nThe incident has raised concerns about safety at Disneyland, with many visitors expressing shock and surprise at the unexpected event. \"You wouldn't expect situations like that coming to a place like this,\" said West Covina resident Jonathan Rosario, who was at the park with a toddler.\n\nDisneyland officials have released a statement saying that they are working closely with local authorities to investigate the incident. \"We take matters like this very seriously and are working closely with local authorities,\" said Disneyland spokeswoman Suzi Brown.\n\nThe incident does not appear to be connected to similar dry-ice explosions in Anaheim in recent months, according to Anaheim police.\n\n**Other News**\n\nIn other news, a probe has been launched into the torture death of a Palmdale boy, and police are investigating two witnesses who dispute Justin Bieber's story about his Ferrari. Additionally, two police officers who took a car on a joyride to Las Vegas have blamed a \"momentary\" lapse for their actions.\n\n**Key Points**\n\n* Christian Barnes, 22, arrested on suspicion of possessing a destructive device\n* Dry ice bomb exploded in Disneyland's Toontown area on Tuesday evening\n* No one was injured in the incident\n* Barnes is cooperating with investigators and is being held on $1 million bail\n* Incident does not appear to be connected to similar dry-ice explosions in Anaheim in recent months\n* Disneyland officials are working closely with local authorities to investigate the incident.",
